{
  "assessment": "The source packet is a physics paper (arXiv:2511.12574v3) presenting a symmetry-based formulation of nonlinear fluctuating hydrodynamics (NFH) in one dimension, with RG analysis and numerical simulations. The extraction focuses on the numerical simulation of the space-time correlation function S^alpha(x,t) for the heat and sound modes, which is the best quantitative cluster with two regimes (heat and sound) sharing the same controls (time t, sound velocity c_s) and readouts (correlation function, dynamical exponent z). The RG fixed point z=3/2 is a theoretical prediction, not a direct control-to-readout relation, so it is captured as a mechanism and claim with symbolic domain. The numerical fits provide quantitative relations: S^alpha(0,t)+C_alpha ~ A_alpha t^{-1/z} with z=3/2, and optimized exponents z=1.52 (heat) and z=1.51 (sound). The source reports fixed parameters (D0=Ds=lambda_i=1, c_s=0.1, L=8192) and robustness checks. The extraction encodes the central-value relations with named parameters, preserving the source's reported values and uncertainty conventions (source_unspecified for fit uncertainties).",
